    <name>
      <text>Inverse Variation 4 - Graph (interactive)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The number of days, \(y\), taken to dig a trench varies inversely as the number of workers, \(x\): \(xy = k\). The graph shows this relationship, and \(P\) is a point on the curve.</p>
[[jsxgraph input-ref-ans2="ans2Ref" width="500px" height="450px"]]
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-1,38,9,-3], axis:true, grid:true, showCopyright:false, showNavigation:false});
var curve = board.create('functiongraph', [function(x){return {#pk#}/x;}, 0.3, 10], {strokeColor:'blue'});
var P = board.create('point', [{#pr#},{#pk/pr#}], {name:'P', fixed:true, color:'red', size:4});
var A = board.create('point', [1,1], {name:'A', snapToGrid:true, snapSizeX:1, snapSizeY:1, size:5});
stack_jxg.bind_point(ans2Ref, A);
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p>(a) Use the point \(P\) (workers, days) to find the constant \(k\).</p>
<p>\(k = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) Drag the point \(A\) to the point on the curve where there are \({@px2@}\) workers. The coordinates of \(A\) appear in the box below.</p>
<p>\(A = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The point \(P\) is \(({@pr@}, {@pk/pr@})\), so \(k = x \times y = {@pr@} \times {@pk/pr@} = {@pk@}\).</p>
<p>The curve is \(y = \frac{ {@pk@} }{x}\). When \(x = {@px2@}\): \(y = \frac{ {@pk@} }{ {@px2@} } = {@pk/px2@}\), so \(A = ({@px2@}, {@pk/px2@})\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
